GameEngine overlay patch for lexbor 3.0.1.

css/selectors: accept :focus-within and :focus-visible pseudo-classes.

lxb_css_selectors_state_pseudo_class() in source/lexbor/css/selectors/state.c
resolves :focus-within (id 0x0e) and :focus-visible (id 0x0d) by name, then
routes them into an explicit "not supported" branch that logs
lxb_css_log_not_supported and returns lxb_css_parser_unexpected_status. That
fails the whole selector, so lexbor discards the entire style rule (no pseudo
node is ever emitted). :focus (0x0c), :hover, :checked and :disabled are absent
from that branch and fall through to `default: break;`, so they are accepted.

The branch exists because lexbor's own DOM selector-matching engine does not
implement these two pseudo-classes. GameEngine never uses that engine: it uses
lexbor only to build the selector AST, then matches with its own cascade engine
(Engine/Modules/UI). Removing the two case labels lets both pseudo-classes fall
through to `default: break;`, parsing as ordinary simple pseudo-classes exactly
like :focus. CSSStylesheetParser.cpp::ConvertPseudoSimple already maps
LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_FOCUS_VISIBLE / _FOCUS_WITHIN to our PseudoClass
kinds, so the AST node is consumed downstream with no further lexbor change.

diff --git a/source/lexbor/css/selectors/state.c b/source/lexbor/css/selectors/state.c
--- a/source/lexbor/css/selectors/state.c
+++ b/source/lexbor/css/selectors/state.c
@@ -1464,8 +1464,6 @@
     switch (pseudo->id) {
         case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_CURRENT:
         case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_DEFAULT:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_FOCUS_VISIBLE:
-        case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_FOCUS_WITHIN:
         case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_FULLSCREEN:
         case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_FUTURE:
         case LXB_CSS_SELECTOR_PSEUDO_CLASS_IN_RANGE:
